# The asset names of a hostkeeper release, one per line, `<version>` standing for X.Y.Z: the
# contract that cargo xtask release (crates/xtask/src/release/contract.rs, asset_names) keeps.
# A name may be added (add it here in the same pull request); a name is never removed or
# renamed, since consumers fetch assets by these names, unless it is withdrawn: a line
# `withdrawn: <name>` is a name a release once held and no longer does, each listed with its reason
# in crates/xtask/src/release/contract/tests.rs (WITHDRAWN). Lines starting with `#` are comments.
# The `hello-` names are the packages and release indexes of the example service, examples/hello, and
# of its failing build (`hello-<version>-fail-ready-*`, the same package started with `--fail-ready`;
# its `.deb`s, `hello_<version>-fail-ready_<arch>.deb`, are the only native packages it has).
# The `mdm-` names are the package and release index of the MDM server stack's service package, built for
# linux-x86_64 only. `hello_<version>_<arch>.deb`, `hello-<version>-macos-arm64.pkg` and `mdm_<version>_amd64.deb` are
# the services' native packages (docs/design/packages-native.md, item A21).
